  "scope": "Synthetic forwarded-email development diagnostics through real normalized inbound capture, forward parsing, suggestion queue boundary, inference, persistence and visibility. No production data or deployment.",
  "observations": [
    "Before the email-policy fix, customer/project context without a new task produced no objects; the other two initial cases passed.",
    "The first revision recovered the objects but one run added redundant task/project relationships. The final policy avoids duplicating parentObjectId links.",
    "Both final runs passed all four cases, including informal customer/project discussion."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Development tuning examples, not independent human validation or fresh held-out evidence.",
    "The baseline contains three cases; final corpus adds an informal-context case and tighter optional relationship scoring. Do not present aggregate percentages as a controlled population-quality comparison.",
    "Runs occurred on dirty development trees before the implementation commit; the reports retain their original revision and dirty flags.",
    "No SMTP/webhook transport verification; a missing production email or job remains a separate diagnosis.",
    "Historical held-out results predate this email policy and must not be reused as fresh evidence for it."
  ],
